# Parsed by Cloudflare Workers static assets (same format as _redirects — the platform
# reads it, never serves it; .assetsignore documents why neither file is listed there).
# Conservative additions ONLY: every header below is safe for every path it matches.
# There is deliberately NO Content-Security-Policy here — the pages load vendored
# scripts, Supabase, esm.sh (three.js), and tenant integrations, and a CSP written
# without a full inventory of those origins would blank real customer traffic.
#
# Rules match the REQUESTED path, before _redirects rewrites — so the pretty routes
# (/admin, /portal, /portal/*) need their own rules alongside the .html filenames.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# index.html (the public designer) is deliberately NOT frame-blocked: tenant host
# pages embed it, and the origin-gated postMessage listener in index.mount.jsx
# ("structureConfig" via ssAllowedOrigin) exists precisely for pages that frame the
# designer. An X-Frame-Options on / would blank every tenant embed — do not add one.

# The portal and the operator console have no framing use left: the Admin-in-portal
# iframe is gone (native since 2026-07-30 — see portal/01-core.jsx, "ADMIN_URL is
# gone"), and admin.html survives only as the standalone break-glass route.
/admin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
/admin.html
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
/portal
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
/portal.html
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
/portal/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

# my-quotes has no framing use either, and it carries customer actions (Accept/Sign)
# behind a localStorage token — exactly the shape clickjacking targets. Both the
# pretty route and the .html spelling need a rule (see the "requested path" note up top).
/my-quotes
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
/my-quotes.html
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
